otc.guide.page.placing_station.title=Set up a restaurant
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step1=Craft and place an order machine, menu board, countertop, chair, packaging shelf, plate shelf and washing sink.
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step2=Equipment links still use a 24-block spherical radius. New machines count other registered, loaded machines -24 to +25 blocks away on every axis (existing minus new, including boundaries). Placement is blocked when that count reaches the global maxOrderMachinesWithin24 (default 1, minimum 1). A diagonal distance over 24 is not enough; a 26-block gap on one axis excludes that machine.
otc.guide.page.placing_station.step3=Place the packaging and plate shelves within five blocks of the countertop; preparation checks those supply distances.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.title=Choose starting dishes
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step1=A new menu board starts with four dishes. Hold a recognizable food and use the board to register another.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step2=Menu registration does not consume food. Each dish adds its nutrition once, not once per item in the held stack.
otc.guide.page.first_menu.step3=Use the board empty-handed or while sneaking to manage dishes from your inventory. The menu holds up to 150 entries.
otc.guide.page.first_order.title=Fulfill your first order
otc.guide.page.first_order.step1=Start trading at the order machine, choose an offer and accept it. A normal order expires 30 minutes after creation.
otc.guide.page.first_order.step2=Obtain the finished dishes listed on the order, place them in your inventory or an accessible refrigerator, and prepare them at the countertop.
otc.guide.page.first_order.step3=Collect the plated meal or parcel from the countertop and use it on the matching customer. Payment and possible tips arrive on delivery.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.title=Read and replace the guide
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step1=You receive this separate Order To Cook handbook on first joining a world. Use it in your hand to open the contents.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step2=Craft another guide with one book and one sheet of paper. It is not the Cookery guide or a replacement for it.
otc.guide.page.guide_access.step3=Browse main chapters, topics and lessons. Use Back, Previous and Next to continue reading.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.title=Manage the menu
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step1=Each menu entry is a finished dish, not a crafting recipe. The countertop cannot cook ingredients into a meal by itself.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step2=Use a held food or the inventory picker. Special items without readable nutrition require an explicit food definition.
otc.guide.page.menu_design.step3=Remove and re-add an entry to adopt updated nutrition or names. Accepted orders keep their original requirements and price.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.title=Nutrition and public variants
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step1=Menu nutrition affects upgrades and income. A generic entry and a specific variant of the same item cannot double-count.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step2=When a food exposes Senluo V1 nativeVariant, variants can be ordered and matched individually. The wrong variant cannot fulfill the order.
otc.guide.page.nutrition_variant.step3=Quality, heat and seasoning are not separate menu identities or price multipliers. Legacy ID-only orders keep working.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.title=Understand order types
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step1=Dine-in orders use plates; delivery orders use parcels and have a destination.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step2=Rush orders have shorter limits and long-distance deliveries travel farther. Walk-in customers require a usable chair.
otc.guide.page.offer_types.step3=Accepting one machine offer cancels its alternatives, but independent walk-in requests remain.
otc.guide.page.timers.title=Timing and expiration
otc.guide.page.timers.step1=New machine offers refresh every ten minutes by default. Normal orders last 30 minutes; rush orders last ten.
otc.guide.page.timers.step2=The clock starts when an order is generated, not accepted. In this version real-time deadlines still pass while away.
otc.guide.page.timers.step3=Expired orders cannot be delivered. A refresh does not erase accepted work or already packed orders.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.title=Coins and restaurant upgrades
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step1=Completed orders pay oTc coins and possible tips. Lifetime earnings are not spendable wallet balance.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step2=The order machine shows the cost and menu nutrition required for the next upgrade, from level 0 up to level 8.
otc.guide.page.money_upgrades.step3=Insufficient nutrition blocks an upgrade. Removing dishes does not erase a purchased level but can lower its benefits.
otc.guide.page.staff.title=Owners and staff
otc.guide.page.staff.step1=The player who places the order machine owns the restaurant and can add staff in its settings.
otc.guide.page.staff.step2=Scripted preparation and stove actions recheck permissions. An already-open native refrigerator cannot be forcibly closed immediately after access is revoked.
otc.guide.page.staff.step3=Do not break active equipment with outstanding orders, plates or pending records. Stop trading and clean up first.
otc.guide.page.countertop.title=Countertop and ingredient handling
otc.guide.page.countertop.step1=The countertop uses finished dishes from your inventory or accessible refrigerators within 24 blocks.
otc.guide.page.countertop.step2=Keep the matching shelf within five blocks and the space above clear. Use a valid order ticket on the countertop to plate or pack that order directly.
otc.guide.page.countertop.step3=Interact empty-handed for one page with dish names, quantities and readiness or shortages. Full requirements must match before items are taken; collect the result from the counter.
otc.guide.page.supplies.title=Packaging and plate shelves
otc.guide.page.supplies.step1=Delivery uses leather from the packaging shelf; dining uses clean plates from the plate shelf. Both must be within five blocks.
otc.guide.page.supplies.step2=The packaging shelf holds ten units; the plate shelf holds 18. Use the matching item on the shelf to refill it.
otc.guide.page.supplies.step3=Dirty plates are not clean supplies. Wash them in a sink or dishwasher before restocking the plate shelf.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.title=Refrigerator compartments
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step1=Interact with the upper 27-slot or lower 54-slot compartment to open its native inventory grid. There is no paginated storage menu.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step2=Sneak and interact empty-handed to compact the selected compartment. Matching item data merges in first-seen order; items never move between compartments. Nearby authorized refrigerators still supply the counter.
otc.guide.page.refrigerator.step3=Bedrock 26.60 and Upcoming Creator Features are required. An upgrade box converts an eligible empty double barrel; check both blocks and inventories first.
otc.guide.page.stove.title=Three-lane stove and fuel
otc.guide.page.stove.step1=Use an ingredient or fuel stack on the stove to deposit it directly. Three lanes share fuel and a 10-second batch; replacing or emptying input resets progress.
otc.guide.page.stove.step2=Interact empty-handed for all seven slots, direct withdrawal, collecting all outputs and refilling. A blocked output affects only its lane.
otc.guide.page.stove.step3=Nine vanilla smoking recipes and two installed Grilling recipes are built in. Suppliers can publish explicit smoking recipes; skewers, mixing and wok dishes stay at their own stations.
otc.guide.page.customer_delivery.title=Customers and handoff
otc.guide.page.customer_delivery.step1=Accepted ordinary dine-in work creates a customer. A chair is preferred, but some regular customers can wait standing.
otc.guide.page.customer_delivery.step2=Walk-in customers require a chair. Keep a usable seat near the restaurant for them. While seated on this pack's chair, attack or mine to cheer for three seconds; sneak to dismount. Cheering only changes animation and sound, not orders.
otc.guide.page.customer_delivery.step3=Use the matching plated meal on the correct customer. A completed order cannot pay out twice.
otc.guide.page.dining_plate.title=Dining plates and pickup
otc.guide.page.dining_plate.step1=Dining progresses through visible stages, and a dirty plate remains after the meal instead of vanishing.
otc.guide.page.dining_plate.step2=Collect the dirty plate from the meal or its supporting table. Clear old plates before serving a new meal at that table. Breaking the plate drops a dirty plate. Collecting with a full inventory also drops it at the meal.
otc.guide.page.dining_plate.step3=Early pickup interrupts the eating animation. Wash collected plates before returning them to the plate shelf. Breaking the plate drops it without interrupting the customer.
otc.guide.page.handwashing.title=Manual washing
otc.guide.page.handwashing.step1=Load a dirty plate into the sink, empty both hands and interact again to begin washing.
otc.guide.page.handwashing.step2=Keep looking at the sink for 80 game ticks (four seconds) to obtain a clean plate. Crosshair feedback shows progress.
otc.guide.page.handwashing.step3=Looking away, leaving or holding an item cancels the wash. The dirty plate remains for another attempt.
otc.guide.page.dishwasher.title=Dishwasher operation
otc.guide.page.dishwasher.step1=Use a dirty plate on the dishwasher to load up to 16 from inventory. An upgrade box converts an eligible empty washing sink.
otc.guide.page.dishwasher.step2=Loaded dishes pass through loading, washing and output stages. Larger batches take longer to wash.
otc.guide.page.dishwasher.step3=When ready, empty both hands and interact to collect the entire clean batch. Insufficient inventory space leaves it inside; return clean plates to the shelf.
otc.guide.page.bagging.title=Pack meals to go
otc.guide.page.bagging.step1=Delivery orders use bags by default. Keep the counter top clear and use the valid ticket to prepare directly, or choose an order empty-handed.
otc.guide.page.bagging.step2=Sneak-click the countertop to choose a bag for a dine-in order. Use leather on the packaging shelf within five blocks; bags keep the original order and leave no dirty plate.
otc.guide.page.bagging.step3=Collect the parcel from the countertop. Its canonical carrier and order proof must match; an ordinary bag or a different carrier cannot replace it.
otc.guide.page.navigation.title=Navigation and delivery
otc.guide.page.navigation.step1=Hold the linked delivery parcel to see destination cues near the crosshair; the parcel also retains coordinates.
otc.guide.page.navigation.step2=Travel to the marked destination and interact with the correct customer using the matching parcel. Long-distance orders need more travel.
otc.guide.page.navigation.step3=Watch the delivery deadline. Prepare transportation for long trips; an expired order cannot be settled.
otc.guide.page.motorcycle.title=Motorcycle basics
otc.guide.page.motorcycle.step1=Use the motorcycle item to place the vehicle and interact to ride. Controls use Bedrock's native vehicle behavior.
otc.guide.page.motorcycle.step2=Sneak-interact with the vehicle for the storage or control panel. It can honk and supports four color variants.
otc.guide.page.motorcycle.step3=Vehicle physics differ from Java. The headlight looks emissive but does not cast real dynamic light.
otc.guide.page.storage.title=Insulated storage and controls
otc.guide.page.storage.step1=The motorcycle includes 54 storage slots, available through its crouch-interaction controls.
otc.guide.page.storage.step2=Track the real order parcel and ticket. Storage does not automatically deliver orders.
otc.guide.page.storage.step3=Use the intended vehicle controls to recover it; do not assume breaking something will preserve stored contents.
otc.guide.page.progress_tracker.title=Personal achievements
otc.guide.page.progress_tracker.step1=This add-on tracks eleven original achievements; ten are implemented. They are not Xbox achievements.
otc.guide.page.progress_tracker.step2=Earnings are attributed to the player who completed the order across restaurants. Spending coins does not reduce lifetime earnings.
otc.guide.page.progress_tracker.step3=Open Personal Progress from this guide for details. Hold use in the air to finish eating an expired parcel and unlock its progression; it restores no hunger.
otc.guide.page.advanced_admin.title=Administrator controls
otc.guide.page.advanced_admin.step1=Owners use the order machine for staff and restaurant settings. Creative players or those tagged otc_admin can use extra controls.
otc.guide.page.advanced_admin.step2=Administrators can register nutrition with ordertocook:food or adjust currency and refresh settings with ordertocook:config.
otc.guide.page.advanced_admin.step3=The administrator test kit is for checking functions, not normal survival. Avoid altering original reward balance for ordinary play.
otc.guide.page.senluo_food.title=Senluo food compatibility
otc.guide.page.senluo_food.step1=Senluo Core V1 can expose quality, heat, seasoning and variants. This guide's add-on reads those fields without rewriting the original item.
otc.guide.page.senluo_food.step2=Public nativeVariant data can identify menu dishes and ingredients. V1 itself does not provide a complete food catalog or nutrition registry.
otc.guide.page.senluo_food.step3=Full Grilling, Tavern and World Liquor recipe and drink integration is pending. Prepare those products at their own stations.
otc.guide.page.limitations.title=Bedrock differences and credits
otc.guide.page.limitations.step1=This is an independent Order To Cook handbook. It uses Bedrock forms and does not change or replace Cookery's guidebook.
otc.guide.page.limitations.step2=Refrigerator compaction follows native Bedrock stack limits; food-only slots and 128-item stacks remain unavailable. Stove and counter controls use single-page panels; player animation and vehicle differences remain.
otc.guide.page.limitations.step3=Maintained by burnt-tea-dev under GPLv3 with credit to original author breezeth. Open Credits and licence from this page.
otc.error.machine_placement_conflict=Cannot place: global machine limit %s reached inside the placement box (-24 to +25 on each axis, existing minus new). Move where fewer registered, loaded machines count; a 26-block gap on one axis excludes that machine.

